  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2610.00003v2</id>
    <title>Retrieval-Augmented Generation
      with   Citation Grounding</title>
    <updated>2026-10-01T12:00:00Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.00003v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.00003v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Large language models hallucinate when answering questions about scientific literature. We
      study retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) that grounds every generated sentence in retrieved
      passages and emits inline citations. Our system combines sparse BM25 retrieval with dense
      embeddings using reciprocal rank fusion. Experiments on three benchmarks show that citation
      precision improves by 12 points over a dense-only baseline.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CL" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.IR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
